---
import '../styles/global.css';
import walkthrough from '../../../../docs/readme/walkthrough.png';
import comments from '../../../../docs/readme/comments.png';
import proof from '../../../../docs/readme/proof.png';

const description =
  'A companion for the coding agents you already run. They publish a walkthrough of what changed. You read it, comment, and decide what to keep.';
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="16x16 32x32 48x48" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/favicon-32.png" sizes="32x32" />
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/apple-touch-icon.png" sizes="180x180" />
    <meta
      name="theme-color"
      content="#ffffff"
      media="(prefers-color-scheme: light)"
    />
    <meta
      name="theme-color"
      content="#171717"
      media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)"
    />
    <title>Porcelain</title>
  </head>
  <body class="bg-background text-foreground font-sans text-base leading-normal tracking-[-0.011em] antialiased">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-8">
      <header class="flex items-baseline justify-between pb-7">
        <div class="font-serif text-lg tracking-[-0.03em]">Porcelain</div>
        <a
          class="text-[13px] text-muted-foreground no-underline"
          href="https://github.com/FabioFiorita/porcelain">Source</a
        >
      </header>

      <h1
        class="max-w-[16ch] font-serif text-[clamp(40px,7vw,58px)] leading-[0.96] font-medium tracking-[-0.035em]"
      >
        <span
          class="block animate-in fade-in slide-in-from-bottom-4 fill-mode-both duration-700"
          >Agents write the code.</span
        >
        <span
          class="block animate-in fade-in slide-in-from-bottom-4 fill-mode-both delay-150 duration-700"
          >This is where you read it.</span
        >
      </h1>
      <p
        class="mt-5 max-w-[38rem] animate-in fade-in slide-in-from-bottom-3 fill-mode-both delay-300 duration-700 text-[17px] leading-snug text-muted-foreground"
      >
        ChatGPT, Claude, Codex and T3 Code keep running. Porcelain is where
        they publish a walkthrough of the change, and where you comment back
        before you keep it.
      </p>
      <div
        class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-2.5 animate-in fade-in fill-mode-both delay-500 duration-700"
      >
        <a
          class="inline-flex h-10 items-center rounded-full bg-foreground px-4 text-sm text-background no-underline"
          href="https://github.com/FabioFiorita/porcelain/releases"
          >Download for Mac</a
        >
        <a
          class="inline-flex h-10 items-center rounded-full px-4 text-sm text-foreground no-underline shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--border)]"
          href="#start">Open in the browser</a
        >
      </div>
      <p class="mt-3.5 text-[13px] text-muted-foreground">
        Apple silicon and any browser. iPhone, iPad and Android are still
        being built.
      </p>

      <figure class="mt-7">
        <div
          class="rounded-[calc(var(--radius)+6px)] bg-card p-2 shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--border)]"
        >
          <img
            class="block w-full rounded-(--radius)"
            src={walkthrough.src}
            width={walkthrough.width}
            height={walkthrough.height}
            alt="A Porcelain review on the decision Revoke access across devices, with its route through the code and the diff underneath"
          />
        </div>
        <figcaption class="mt-2.5 text-[13px] text-muted-foreground">
          One decision, the route it takes, and the diff under the note that
          explains it.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <section class="mt-10 grid gap-6">
        <article class="grid grid-cols-[28px_1fr] gap-3" data-animate>
          <div class="pt-1 text-xs text-muted-foreground tabular-nums">01</div>
          <div>
            <h2
              class="font-serif text-[26px] leading-tight font-medium tracking-[-0.03em]"
            >
              A walkthrough, in the order the change runs.
            </h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
              The agent publishes a briefing, then one stop for each decision.
              Numbered notes land on the lines they explain. You mark the
              decision read, and the files it shows go with it.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="grid grid-cols-[28px_1fr] gap-3" data-animate>
          <div class="pt-1 text-xs text-muted-foreground tabular-nums">02</div>
          <div>
            <h2
              class="font-serif text-[26px] leading-tight font-medium tracking-[-0.03em]"
            >
              What the story left out stays visible.
            </h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
              Changed lines no decision covers are Not explained: a stop of
              their own, and marks inside the files you already opened. A
              path-sorted diff leaves that work at the bottom of a long list.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="grid grid-cols-[28px_1fr] gap-3" data-animate>
          <div class="pt-1 text-xs text-muted-foreground tabular-nums">03</div>
          <div>
            <h2
              class="font-serif text-[26px] leading-tight font-medium tracking-[-0.03em]"
            >
              A comment the agent can answer.
            </h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
              You write on the file. The reply comes back in the same thread,
              through MCP, on your machine. The agent stays in the app you
              already pay for.
            </p>
            <figure class="mt-4">
              <div
                class="rounded-[calc(var(--radius)+6px)] bg-card p-2 shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--border)]"
              >
                <img
                  class="block w-full rounded-(--radius)"
                  src={comments.src}
                  width={comments.width}
                  height={comments.height}
                  alt="A reviewer comment and the agent's reply in the same Porcelain thread"
                />
              </div>
            </figure>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="grid grid-cols-[28px_1fr] gap-3" data-animate>
          <div class="pt-1 text-xs text-muted-foreground tabular-nums">04</div>
          <div>
            <h2
              class="font-serif text-[26px] leading-tight font-medium tracking-[-0.03em]"
            >
              The proof it attached.
            </h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
              Checks and images sit beside how far you have read. Porcelain
              shows what the agent reported, next to the review, so a claim
              has a trail.
            </p>
            <figure class="mt-4">
              <div
                class="rounded-[calc(var(--radius)+6px)] bg-card p-2 shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--border)]"
              >
                <img
                  class="block w-full rounded-(--radius)"
                  src={proof.src}
                  width={proof.width}
                  height={proof.height}
                  alt="Proof with check results, an image, and the readiness panel"
                />
              </div>
            </figure>
          </div>
        </article>
      </section>

      <section
        class="mt-9 grid grid-cols-1 gap-2.5 sm:grid-cols-3"
        aria-label="Where Porcelain runs"
      >
        <div
          class="rounded-(--radius) bg-card p-4 shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--border)]"
        >
          <strong class="block text-sm font-medium">Browser</strong>
          <span
            class="mt-1.5 block text-[13px] leading-snug text-muted-foreground"
            >The same review, from the server on your machine.</span
          >
        </div>
        <div
          class="rounded-(--radius) bg-card p-4 shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--border)]"
        >
          <strong class="block text-sm font-medium">Mac</strong>
          <span
            class="mt-1.5 block text-[13px] leading-snug text-muted-foreground"
            >The app around that review. Apple silicon today.</span
          >
        </div>
        <div
          class="rounded-(--radius) bg-card p-4 shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--border)]"
        >
          <strong class="block text-sm font-medium">Phone and iPad</strong>
          <span
            class="mt-1.5 block text-[13px] leading-snug text-muted-foreground"
            >The seat we are building. It appears here when you can hold it.</span
          >
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-9" id="start">
        <h2
          class="font-serif text-[26px] leading-tight font-medium tracking-[-0.03em]"
        >
          On the machine that holds the repositories.
        </h2>
        <pre
          class="mt-3.5 overflow-auto rounded-(--radius) bg-card p-4 font-mono text-[13px] leading-snug text-foreground shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--border)]">npx @fabiofiorita/porcelain@latest serve</pre>
        <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
          Pair the browser with the link it prints, then open the repository.
        </p>
      </section>

      <footer
        class="mt-9 flex justify-between pt-4 text-[13px] text-muted-foreground shadow-[inset_0_1px_0_var(--border)]"
      >
        <span>MIT</span>
        <span>One server. Your agents. Your machine.</span>
      </footer>
    </div>
    <script>
      const reduce = matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
      const frames = document.querySelectorAll('[data-animate]');
      const show = (frame) => {
        if (reduce) return;
        frame.classList.add(
          'animate-in',
          'fade-in',
          'slide-in-from-bottom-3',
          'duration-700',
          'fill-mode-both',
        );
      };
      if (!('IntersectionObserver' in window)) {
        frames.forEach(show);
      } else {
        const io = new IntersectionObserver(
          (entries) => {
            for (const entry of entries) {
              if (!entry.isIntersecting) continue;
              show(entry.target);
              io.unobserve(entry.target);
            }
          },
          { threshold: 0.25 },
        );
        frames.forEach((frame) => io.observe(frame));
      }
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
